    "description": "Lists this project's dev servers: which are running (name, port, pid, uptime, and the log file when it was started from the Servers pane) and which known start commands (package.json scripts, .claude/launch.json, Procfile) are not running. With all: true it also lists every other TCP listener on this machine, with its port and process. Use it instead of running lsof, netstat, ss or ps in Bash to learn what is listening on which port, whether a dev server is up, or who holds a port: it answers from a scan every open session shares, where lsof alone can take 10s or more on a loaded machine. Read-only: it never starts, stops or restarts anything; the person does that with the Start, Stop and Restart buttons of the Servers pane (/servers)."
